WEBVTT

00:04.504 --> 00:05.463
Don't shoot, Stan!

00:08.967 --> 00:11.553
Dr. Taiju was a decoy…

00:13.430 --> 00:14.848
<i>The enemy's actual leader…</i>

00:15.890 --> 00:18.059
<i>is a skilled scientist named…</i>

00:20.270 --> 00:21.354
Senku.

00:22.689 --> 00:25.108
It's Senku Ishigami.

00:26.401 --> 00:28.278
A sniper! There's a sniper!

00:28.361 --> 00:30.280
-What?
-What?

00:31.614 --> 00:32.699
<i>Did they discover us?</i>

00:33.992 --> 00:35.910
<i>Fool! Don't look at me, Luna!</i>

00:36.661 --> 00:38.455
<i>You'll expose the sniper!</i>

00:40.123 --> 00:41.207
<i>No, wait…</i>

00:42.208 --> 00:43.209
<i>Look at me!</i>

00:44.419 --> 00:46.463
<i>Who's the skilled scientist leader,</i>

00:46.546 --> 00:49.716
<i>the hot-headed guy among these three?</i>

00:49.799 --> 00:53.595
<i>If the target's</i>
<i>as hot-headed as Xeno says,</i>

00:53.678 --> 00:54.971
<i>he'll certainly…</i>

00:55.055 --> 00:58.850
<i>follow your gaze, Luna,</i>
<i>and then look at me</i>

00:59.392 --> 01:00.935
<i>instinctively…</i>

01:02.020 --> 01:03.354
<i>He'll be flushed out.</i>

01:04.773 --> 01:07.484
<i>Hi, Senku Ishigami.</i>

01:09.694 --> 01:11.946
Xeno, I'm going to ask you

01:12.572 --> 01:13.948
one last time…

01:15.992 --> 01:19.954
Are you sure you want me to kill him?

01:23.333 --> 01:24.292
Go ahead.

01:25.084 --> 01:26.503
Do it.

01:40.517 --> 01:44.896
ORIGINAL WORK: RIICHIRO INAGAKI, BOICHI
SHUEISHA "JUMP COMICS"

03:18.489 --> 03:21.200
-Are those gunshots?
-The bullets are coming!

03:21.784 --> 03:24.454
No! They'll hit before we even hear them!

03:26.164 --> 03:28.333
<i>They've already been fired.</i>

03:35.673 --> 03:39.344
Senku!

03:53.775 --> 03:55.568
It's done.

03:55.652 --> 03:59.155
I got the enemy scientist leader.

04:01.324 --> 04:03.117
Don't fall behind, you two.

04:04.535 --> 04:05.745
We're on the lookout.

04:05.828 --> 04:08.289
But what about my lady?

04:08.373 --> 04:12.168
Leave her or save her, that's up to you.

04:12.252 --> 04:13.920
She was not part of my mission.

04:14.003 --> 04:17.298
Damn you!

04:18.508 --> 04:19.842
My lady…

04:21.302 --> 04:24.681
<i>What do I do?</i>

04:26.391 --> 04:29.936
They've murdered Senku!

04:32.272 --> 04:33.147
Don't panic!

04:33.940 --> 04:36.276
The enemy will let their guard down now,

04:36.359 --> 04:38.528
thinking that they're now unassailable

04:38.611 --> 04:41.281
after getting rid
of our scientific leader.

04:41.364 --> 04:44.158
They're thinking that making us surrender

04:44.242 --> 04:46.703
will be a piece of cake!

04:46.786 --> 04:49.580
It's our chance to counterattack!
Don't you think?

04:52.875 --> 04:55.628
You have a point.

04:55.712 --> 04:57.297
We know, but…

04:57.380 --> 05:00.216
I wouldn't call this a chance.

05:00.300 --> 05:02.176
At least not under these circumstances.

05:02.260 --> 05:03.928
He's right.

05:04.012 --> 05:06.514
At least we should prepare
Senku's grave first…

05:08.891 --> 05:10.101
Don't jump to conclusions!

05:18.067 --> 05:19.986
"I won't die, idiots."

05:25.700 --> 05:27.952
"The bullets came out smoothly."

05:28.036 --> 05:29.579
That's what he's saying.

05:32.248 --> 05:36.461
Don't force yourself to talk, Senku!
You need to rest!

05:36.544 --> 05:39.005
What a relief! He made it narrowly--

05:39.088 --> 05:40.465
With all due respect…

05:40.548 --> 05:44.052
Keep your voice down,
or the enemy will hear you!

05:44.135 --> 05:47.263
It appears that he stopped the bullets

05:47.346 --> 05:49.807
with this water and powder bag.

05:52.560 --> 05:55.104
It truly is impressive!

05:56.939 --> 05:58.024
"Yes."

05:58.107 --> 06:01.569
"Had it been the head, I would have
ten billion percent died instantly."

06:02.653 --> 06:06.449
"I could be the only person
who knows the Revival Fluid recipe."

06:07.116 --> 06:10.703
"I bet the enemy wanted to give me
enough time to write it down."

06:11.621 --> 06:14.707
"I could tell he was…"

06:15.208 --> 06:16.459
"going for my chest."

06:17.168 --> 06:20.379
That's what he said.
In English, that would be:

06:20.463 --> 06:24.425
"If it was a headshot,
it would have been an instant death."

06:24.509 --> 06:26.719
Those are amazing
simultaneous interpreting skills!

06:26.803 --> 06:28.554
So don't force yourself to talk!

06:29.931 --> 06:32.100
Amazing…

06:32.183 --> 06:34.477
<i>He had thought it all out…</i>

06:36.979 --> 06:38.481
<i>even in his condition…</i>

06:41.984 --> 06:42.860
He fainted!

06:43.694 --> 06:45.404
So he really is seriously injured?

06:45.488 --> 06:47.115
I'll administer emergency treatment.

06:47.740 --> 06:51.869
But still, he won't make it
without the help of a doctor.

07:05.925 --> 07:09.679
<i>I really, really only have</i>
<i>a faint memory of it, but…</i>

07:10.430 --> 07:12.432
<i>Squeezing his upper arm</i>

07:13.349 --> 07:15.685
<i>would cause the pulse in his wrist</i>
<i>to fade away.</i>

07:15.768 --> 07:16.644
LOW BLOOD PRESSURE
HIGH BLOOD PRESSURE

07:16.727 --> 07:19.105
<i>If it fades with a slight press,</i>
<i>his blood pressure is low.</i>

07:19.689 --> 07:22.692
<i>If a stronger press is needed,</i>
<i>then his blood pressure is high.</i>

07:23.276 --> 07:25.403
<i>That way, we can somehow measure</i>

07:26.654 --> 07:28.072
if his blood pressure is dropping.

07:28.156 --> 07:29.198
Luna…

07:29.824 --> 07:30.825
Are you a doctor?

07:31.409 --> 07:34.954
No, no! I'm too young to be one!

07:36.789 --> 07:39.208
I was just a student…

07:39.709 --> 07:41.002
in medicine.

07:45.840 --> 07:47.800
<i>I'll become Luna, the mighty woman,</i>

07:47.884 --> 07:50.261
<i>and then I'll date</i>
<i>a smart and handsome man.</i>

07:51.929 --> 07:55.349
<i>I tried hard and paid attention in class</i>

07:55.933 --> 07:57.018
<i>so no one could tell me</i>

07:57.101 --> 08:00.480
<i>that I just got in</i>
<i>because of Dad's connections.</i>

08:00.980 --> 08:03.232
<i>But I couldn’t understand a thing</i>

08:03.316 --> 08:05.818
<i>and ended up being the only student</i>
<i>who dropped out.</i>

08:07.695 --> 08:08.738
Please!

08:09.906 --> 08:11.449
I beg you, Luna!

08:12.158 --> 08:14.911
There's… no one else…

08:17.580 --> 08:18.831
No one else…

08:20.583 --> 08:21.918
Please…

08:23.044 --> 08:24.837
Help Senku…

08:25.922 --> 08:28.674
Save our friend… Save him…

08:41.020 --> 08:42.647
Damn…

08:43.397 --> 08:45.441
No matter where we charge from,

08:45.525 --> 08:47.860
we'll be completely exposed.

08:48.819 --> 08:51.656
We'll end up getting showered
with arrows and be done for.

08:51.739 --> 08:52.657
Yes.

08:52.740 --> 08:55.326
We'd still have a chance
if they were actual arrows.

08:55.409 --> 08:59.539
But wouldn't we be killed instantly
in a machine-gun crossfire?

08:59.622 --> 09:00.665
That's bad.

09:00.748 --> 09:04.252
They really are the Kingdom of Science.

09:14.720 --> 09:17.348
Once again, we've got
an extremely reliable team!

09:18.099 --> 09:20.393
You knew we were here, right?

09:20.977 --> 09:23.229
We followed the trail that Gen marked

09:23.896 --> 09:25.356
<i>by scattering his flowers.</i>

09:27.775 --> 09:29.569
That's the enemy base, isn't it?

09:30.444 --> 09:33.114
We were planning to get the corn at night…

09:34.949 --> 09:36.951
but the field was too wide open.

09:37.785 --> 09:41.080
The lake is close by,
but there are no covers at all.

09:41.664 --> 09:44.917
If only we could
sneak into the enemy fortress…

09:45.001 --> 09:47.378
We wouldn't lose in hand-to-hand combat.

09:47.461 --> 09:49.672
However,
securing the enemy boss, Dr. Xeno,

09:49.755 --> 09:53.050
and being able to escape
is a totally different story.

09:54.635 --> 09:56.262
Maybe digging is our only option.

09:57.346 --> 09:58.639
It appears so.

09:59.682 --> 10:02.268
-Digging?
-Really?

10:05.646 --> 10:07.064
<i>It works in both directions.</i>

10:07.815 --> 10:10.401
<i>An underground route</i>
<i>that will let us infiltrate.</i>

10:11.360 --> 10:13.029
<i>We'll make a tunnel.</i>

10:13.112 --> 10:15.364
Awesome!

10:15.448 --> 10:18.784
That sounds terrible.

10:19.368 --> 10:23.873
We'll have to ask Senku
for heavy-duty drilling equipment

10:23.956 --> 10:25.750
and anything else we might need.

10:26.709 --> 10:27.960
Yes.

10:29.962 --> 10:33.257
Speaking of which, Perseus is calling.

10:34.258 --> 10:37.136
<i>43, 32…</i>

10:37.928 --> 10:38.763
<i>33…</i>

10:40.014 --> 10:42.683
What's with these weird numbers
all of a sudden?

10:42.767 --> 10:44.935
Is Ryusui kidding?

10:45.019 --> 10:46.270
It's the Uesugi Cipher.

10:46.354 --> 10:47.563
<i>57…</i>

10:47.647 --> 10:49.357
The Sengoku-era military commander,

10:49.440 --> 10:51.984
Kenshin Uesugi,
used this ciphering method.

10:52.068 --> 10:54.236
The mechanism is very simple.

10:54.320 --> 10:57.698
We use the numbers from the <i>Iroha</i> chart
to communicate words.

10:58.366 --> 11:01.160
As slick as Dr. Xeno can be,

11:01.243 --> 11:04.580
only the Japanese know
about the <i>Iroha</i> poem.

11:06.499 --> 11:09.293
It's an incredibly old-school cipher
compared to the enemy's.

11:09.377 --> 11:11.837
But it's simple, yet effective.

11:11.921 --> 11:14.715
Longer messages will be analyzed
by character frequency.

11:15.299 --> 11:18.469
And what are they trying to say
with that cipher?

11:18.552 --> 11:23.099
<i>63, 57, 24…</i>

11:23.182 --> 11:24.517
Senku…

11:25.267 --> 11:26.268
has been shot!

11:29.855 --> 11:32.441
Don't worry. It looks like he's alive.

11:34.360 --> 11:35.820
But,

11:35.903 --> 11:40.032
it looks like it's not the best time
to ask for scientific items, is it?

11:40.950 --> 11:43.285
Still, digging is the only plan we have.

11:43.369 --> 11:45.329
In that case, we'll do it without science!

11:48.082 --> 11:49.792
There's a message from Senku.

11:50.376 --> 11:52.002
It's just three characters.

11:53.129 --> 11:54.797
47…

11:55.714 --> 11:57.425
12…

11:58.217 --> 12:00.094
42.

12:02.513 --> 12:03.639
<i>Chrome…</i>

12:23.325 --> 12:26.704
You'll understand, right?

12:30.749 --> 12:33.669
<i>No matter the circumstances for us humans.</i>

12:33.752 --> 12:37.506
<i>I'm ten billion percent sure</i>
<i>there will always be someone</i>

12:38.007 --> 12:42.136
<i>who wants to know</i>
<i>how everything works in this world!</i>

12:45.055 --> 12:47.933
You're a scientist…

12:49.518 --> 12:52.021
<i>Dr. Chrome…</i>

13:01.989 --> 13:04.116
<i>We will make a secret tunnel</i>

13:04.867 --> 13:07.828
<i>to the enemy base, where Dr. Xeno is,</i>

13:08.787 --> 13:10.331
<i>with the power of science.</i>

13:11.957 --> 13:14.543
<i>But Senku's been shot and needs to rest.</i>

13:15.211 --> 13:16.629
<i>Who will take his place?</i>

13:18.005 --> 13:20.716
<i>Can I really do that?</i>

13:21.300 --> 13:23.761
<i>The one they called a sorcerer</i>
<i>just for changing the color of fire,</i>

13:24.470 --> 13:25.304
<i>me?</i>

13:27.431 --> 13:28.724
<i>No.</i>

13:31.185 --> 13:33.729
<i>It's not about if I can or not.</i>
<i>There's just no one else!</i>

13:35.189 --> 13:37.233
<i>I'm Chrome, the science-user.</i>

13:38.150 --> 13:40.444
I'll make it all!

13:40.528 --> 13:42.530
Starting from the roadmap!

13:46.742 --> 13:48.994
We'll need some time.

13:50.371 --> 13:51.956
At least two weeks.

13:56.293 --> 13:59.046
Dr. Xeno's minions have taken down Senku,

13:59.129 --> 14:01.465
so now he believes
he's eliminated a scientific threat.

14:02.174 --> 14:05.344
Thus, they'll come to ask us
to surrender at any time.

14:05.928 --> 14:08.138
Surrender? Are they idiots?

14:08.222 --> 14:09.473
There's no way we'll do that.

14:10.057 --> 14:13.936
But what can we do
if they keep pushing us?

14:14.019 --> 14:16.063
Just like Hyoga said,

14:16.146 --> 14:19.149
they'll likely charge at us
with fast pirate ships.

14:19.733 --> 14:23.904
We don't know if that will happen
tomorrow or in a month.

14:24.613 --> 14:27.324
That's why a forceful approach is risky.

14:27.408 --> 14:29.243
It will be wise to take our time.

14:29.827 --> 14:32.913
All we have to do is tilt
the enemy's balance in that direction.

14:33.539 --> 14:34.498
Right?

14:39.461 --> 14:41.422
"Time to build it immediately."

14:42.256 --> 14:45.259
"Ukyo has the real Medusa right now."

14:46.260 --> 14:49.763
"It will be our special present
to Dr. Xeno."

14:49.847 --> 14:52.641
What?

15:00.691 --> 15:01.984
What is this?

15:03.944 --> 15:06.488
Why did you give it to him?

15:06.572 --> 15:08.532
It was Medusa, our special weapon!

15:08.616 --> 15:10.117
It was out of battery anyway.

15:10.200 --> 15:11.952
But, seriously…

15:14.246 --> 15:15.664
I see!

15:16.457 --> 15:18.500
<i>A scientist like Dr. Xeno</i>

15:18.584 --> 15:21.170
<i>will understand immediately</i>
<i>when he sees the real thing.</i>

15:21.837 --> 15:25.925
<i>It's a super-advanced scientific object</i>
<i>far beyond 21st-century levels.</i>

15:26.508 --> 15:28.594
Do you think that will pressure them?

15:29.386 --> 15:31.472
It's pointless to worry about that.

15:31.555 --> 15:33.682
Of course,
there'll be a fake commentator too.

15:33.766 --> 15:34.642
Who?

15:36.393 --> 15:37.811
You mean,

15:37.895 --> 15:40.522
reading the situation and lying smoothly?

15:40.606 --> 15:43.525
"This is a petrification weapon.
There are more of them!"

15:43.609 --> 15:45.152
Do I have to bluff like that?

15:45.235 --> 15:49.406
But the only person who can do that
is in the enemy's camp, you know why…

15:51.408 --> 15:53.035
Is that by any chance

15:53.118 --> 15:55.663
a petrification device?

15:58.749 --> 16:02.169
Do you know it, Mr. Gen?

16:06.340 --> 16:07.925
That's what happened

16:08.008 --> 16:09.760
on the southern island.

16:09.843 --> 16:13.013
I picked up plenty of them!

16:13.097 --> 16:15.933
It's an ancient anachronical artifact.

16:16.016 --> 16:20.270
Fortunately, the thing that just
dropped on us seems to be a dud.

16:20.354 --> 16:22.940
But if it were to explode,
all of us who are here

16:23.023 --> 16:26.527
would turn into stone! It'd be terrible!

16:27.111 --> 16:29.822
<i>I hope this will be enough, Senku.</i>

16:29.905 --> 16:33.325
<i>There's no reason to hand over</i>
<i>the real petrification device so suddenly,</i>

16:33.409 --> 16:35.202
<i>unless it's just for a bluff.</i>

16:37.121 --> 16:39.623
That bat guy is
totally bluffing, isn't he?

16:40.207 --> 16:43.127
The information about the leader
was a lie, wasn't it?

16:43.210 --> 16:45.170
What Dr. Taiju?

16:45.254 --> 16:46.422
It was Dr. Senku!

16:47.881 --> 16:49.383
For real?

16:49.466 --> 16:50.718
I was tricked!

16:50.801 --> 16:53.804
Those two were always together,
so someone must have set me up!

16:54.388 --> 16:58.225
So the brilliant scientist
was Senku all along!

17:01.061 --> 17:03.480
Let's put aside Mr. Gen's credibility.

17:04.231 --> 17:06.233
This elegant machine…

17:06.316 --> 17:10.237
There's no doubt that it surpasses
the technology of the old world.

17:10.863 --> 17:14.199
How is it activated,
how long does it take,

17:14.283 --> 17:15.617
and what’s its range?

17:16.410 --> 17:18.579
You're back, Stanley!

17:21.749 --> 17:24.460
Excuse me, Stanley.

17:24.543 --> 17:28.964
Only the battle team's leader
knows the details.

17:29.048 --> 17:31.216
The only thing I know is…

17:31.925 --> 17:36.597
Just like that petrifying ray
from thousands of years ago,

17:36.680 --> 17:38.891
it's inevitable!

17:38.974 --> 17:42.853
If we rush in and attack the ship,
we might all end up petrified!

17:47.900 --> 17:49.943
It's an unknown science, after all.

17:50.027 --> 17:53.030
We have no way to verify the truth.

17:53.113 --> 17:55.324
In any case…

18:03.832 --> 18:05.292
What the hell?

18:05.375 --> 18:08.420
You're too noisy! Are you singing?

18:08.504 --> 18:10.422
You're tone-deaf! Awful!

18:10.506 --> 18:13.175
This is the most deadly
weapon of destruction,

18:13.258 --> 18:15.677
isn't it?

18:19.765 --> 18:22.935
Is that thing still not ready?

18:23.727 --> 18:25.229
Once it's finished…

18:25.312 --> 18:28.982
I won't have the time
to dispose of the petrification ray,

18:29.066 --> 18:31.693
if there is one.

18:31.777 --> 18:35.739
I can just take control
over their ship right away.

18:36.448 --> 18:37.616
Dr. Brody!

18:38.534 --> 18:42.496
I'm counting on your golden right arm,
my genius mechanic.

18:42.579 --> 18:45.207
When will it be finished?

18:45.290 --> 18:48.001
In a month? In half a year?

18:51.380 --> 18:53.674
Don't talk like that, little brat!

18:54.633 --> 18:56.301
Two weeks.

18:56.385 --> 18:58.303
It will be ready in two weeks.

18:58.387 --> 19:00.222
Perfect.

19:00.305 --> 19:02.933
That's actually an elegant answer.

19:04.810 --> 19:07.855
<i>So, this is something you</i>
<i>want to hide from me, huh?</i>

19:07.938 --> 19:11.358
<i>They're making something…</i>

19:11.441 --> 19:13.277
<i>A secret scientific item</i>

19:13.360 --> 19:18.073
<i>that none of Senku and the others</i>
<i>could have imagined.</i>

19:19.032 --> 19:22.327
<i>For now, it seems like</i>
<i>I managed to buy some time.</i>

19:23.662 --> 19:26.331
<i>But while I was buying time,</i>

19:26.415 --> 19:28.959
<i>I was presented</i>
<i>with the enemy's technology.</i>

19:31.712 --> 19:34.840
<i>This is a time-limited…</i>

19:41.388 --> 19:44.850
<i>science vs. science craft showdown!</i>

19:45.434 --> 19:46.351
Hey!

19:47.144 --> 19:49.646
I won't be able to do it just by myself!

19:50.355 --> 19:51.857
I'll need all of your help.

19:51.940 --> 19:54.693
At your service!

20:00.407 --> 20:04.494
Can you gauge anything just by peering
into the enemy's camp from this distance?

20:05.287 --> 20:07.247
It's called triangulation.

20:07.331 --> 20:10.375
Just by looking at
the length and angle of a line,

20:10.459 --> 20:13.712
you can calculate the digging distance
without even going to the site.

20:14.213 --> 20:18.634
I'll add this number to this one…
No, multiply it…

20:18.717 --> 20:20.510
And then…

20:23.889 --> 20:25.182
Arithmetic?

20:25.265 --> 20:28.268
Chrome, I remember when you
challenged Senku to an arithmetic contest

20:28.352 --> 20:30.395
and got completely defeated.

20:30.479 --> 20:34.149
I didn't pick up much
beyond the multiplication tables.

20:34.233 --> 20:37.027
I've improved since, but barely.

20:39.947 --> 20:43.200
-Amazing!
-This looks quite complex!

20:43.283 --> 20:46.828
It starts now. There's still more to come!

21:03.720 --> 21:05.305
And this will top it off!

21:07.099 --> 21:10.060
<i>I'm Chrome, the science-user!</i>

21:13.063 --> 21:15.190
All right, it's done!

21:15.941 --> 21:17.693
Dr. Chrome's first invention!

21:18.860 --> 21:21.238
An original roadmap!

21:24.157 --> 21:28.495
My biggest, baddest idea is this!

21:28.578 --> 21:30.998
CONSTRUCTION MINING ROTARY LOOP KNIFE

21:31.915 --> 21:34.918
<i>It can spin and dig tunnels automatically!</i>

21:35.002 --> 21:38.839
<i>I bet that 21st-century science</i>
<i>never came up with this idea!</i>

21:39.423 --> 21:43.927
"Construction Mining Rotary Loop Knife"?

21:44.011 --> 21:46.430
Yes! Let's name it that.

21:46.513 --> 21:47.848
CONSTRUCTION MINING ROTARY

21:47.931 --> 21:48.807
LOOP KNIFE

21:49.766 --> 21:50.600
It's a drill.

21:53.103 --> 21:54.396
It was already invented!

21:57.983 --> 21:59.234
By using this…

22:00.944 --> 22:02.487
We'll be able to dig into the ground.

22:03.196 --> 22:04.281
All right!

22:04.906 --> 22:06.783
Let's attack all at once!

22:07.367 --> 22:09.453
Let's get to the enemy's base…

22:11.913 --> 22:14.541
<i>with the science I created!</i>

23:53.348 --> 23:55.976
